Short: Filters email by configurable headers (1.5)
Version: 1.5
Requires: OS 2.04 and a filesystem supporting filechange notification
Uploader: mhunter@andrew.cmu.edu (Matthew Hunter)
Author: mhunter@andrew.cmu.edu (Matthew Hunter)
Type: comm/mail
Replaces: filter.lha

News: Because the development of anything worth releasing beyond 141 has
		taken so long, I decided to go ahead and release this version,
		which is basically collected bugfixes and a few minor improvements.
		Later versions are still in flux, but *will* happen eventually.

History:
Filter v1.0: First public release.
		 v1.0a: Fixed a bug in the .guide file
		 v1.1: Added a quick and dirty DELAY option.  Not released.
		 v1.2: Not released.
		 v1.3: Public release:
				 * Improved speed significantly
				 * Added delete, forward, command capability
				 * Added proper command-line options, including DELAY
				 * Added Workbench startup code (inc. tooltype options)
				 * Increased code size slightly ;)
				 * Added installer script
		 v1.4: Public Release (primarily bugfixes)
				 * Fixed enforcer hit
				 * Now it -really- searches on the Subject: header
				 * GUI config editor, courtesy of "TTT"
		 v1.41:Public Bugfix Release
				 * Got an 060, nailed remaining enforcer hits
		 v1.5: Incremental Release (collected bugfixes, very minor features)
				 * Fixed several possible enforcer hits
				 * Searches Newsgroups: header (by request)
				 * Increased mailbox parsing intelligence slightly
       v1.5a: Released source.  Development of this version dead.
       v1.5b: Bugfix release (2026), made from the archived source
				 * Mail delivered while filtering is no longer lost
				 * Fixed buffer overflows, memory leaks, and heavy stack use
				 * Messages are copied whole, so folders stay valid mailboxes
				 * Newsgroups: no longer carries over between messages
				 * Source compiles again (with gcc; SAS/C not tested)
